  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1235 AM MST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nBrief upper ridge across the area on Thu will bring dry and mild\nconditions, then next fast-moving upper trough approaches the\narea late in the day. System will spread snow showers to the \nContinental Divide beginning Thu night, with best window for \nprecip during the day on Fri. System continues to track fairly \nfar north, which will limit precip away from the Divide, though \na least a few ensemble members hint at some energy hanging back \nin the base of the trough late Fri into Sat, which could at \nleast keep some high terrain snow showers going into Sat \nmorning. Accumulating snow again looks heaviest over the ern San\nJuans (4-6 inches), with lighter amounts (1-3 inches) farther \nnorth in the central mountains. Winds will be gusty all \nlocations again during the day Friday into Friday evening, with \nat least some guidance suggesting gusts over 60 mph spreading \nfrom the mountains through the San Luis Valley and southern I-25\ncorridor late in the day. Bulk of Sat into Sun then looks dry \nand cool, before showers return early next week as still another\ntrough approaches the region.",
